{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And Jacob's anger was kindled</b> — For the prayer of the righteous is not in their hand to be heard and answered in every case. And because she spoke in the manner of the entreaties of beloved women, to frighten him with [the threat of] her death, his anger was kindled. Therefore he told her that he is not in the place of Elohim, who visits barrenness in every case, and he is not at fault in the matter, for the fruit of the womb was withheld from her and not from him — and this was to discipline her and put her to shame. Now the righteous woman, upon seeing that she could not rely on Jacob's prayer, turned to pray for herself before the One who hears cry; and this is \"And Elohim hearkened to her\" (Genesis 30:22). And perhaps it may be corrected according to the opinion of our Sages, that Jacob — it is impossible that he did not pray for his beloved wife when she was barren, but his prayer was not accepted. And now Rachel came to pressure him, saying that he should give her children in any case through his prayer, for he is no less than his father, who did so. And his anger was kindled and he told her that the matter is in the hand of Elohim and not in his hand; and his father's prayer was heard because he was a righteous man and destined to have seed, but she — the fruit of the womb was withheld from her. And this is correct."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:48.096485240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}